{"id":1175,"date":"2020-11-23T13:19:59","date_gmt":"2020-11-23T21:19:59","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1175"},"modified":"2024-09-01T20:24:30","modified_gmt":"2024-09-02T03:24:30","slug":"codrone-arduino-leds","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-leds\/","title":{"rendered":"CoDrone LEDs"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215d18879f\" name=\"6a2215d18879f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LED settings<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The easiest way to change your LEDs is to do it in void setup. This will change the LEDs&#8217; colors and patterns before your program actually starts.\u00a0There are thirteen(!) different combinations to set your color and patterns, and they all have this format:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">setLED(Color, Mode, Interval)<\/pre>\n<p>OR<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">setLED(R, G, B, Mode, Interval)<\/pre>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"activity2__spacer\">\n<div class=\"activity2__question\">\n<div class=\"styled-checkbox activity2__button-checkbox\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215d1888d6\" name=\"6a2215d1888d6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Function options<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Each LED function changes the LEDs on a different part of your CoDrone. These are your options:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">setEyeLED<\/code>: changes the eyes&#8217; LEDs<\/li>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">setArmLED<\/code>: changes the arms&#8217; LEDs<\/li>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">setAllLED<\/code>: changes the eyes&#8217; and arms&#8217; LEDs<\/li>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">setEyeDefaultLED<\/code>: changes the eyes&#8217; LEDs to the default<\/li>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">setArmDefaultLED<\/code>: changes the arms&#8217; LEDs to the default<\/li>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">setAllDefaultLED<\/code>: changes the eyes&#8217; and arms&#8217; LEDs to the default<\/li>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">resetDefaultLED<\/code>: resets your CoDrone&#8217;s LEDs<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215d18893f\" name=\"6a2215d18893f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Color options<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Within the LED functions, there are a couple of ways to pick your color:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>You can type it in directly using names from\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/open?id=1LD4Rif4ztcW9fnQfGZtYZn4kHaXjXN17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-link-type=\"LINK\">this document<\/a>.<\/li>\n<li>You can use RGB values to get a more precise color. RGB stands for red, green, and blue and all three can have values from 0 to 255. Any color values can be found on an RGB table\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.rapidtables.com\/web\/color\/RGB_Color.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-link-type=\"LINK\">like this one<\/a>. Instead of typing in the color&#8217;s name, you can type in the three values that come up with commas in between.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215d1889a8\" name=\"6a2215d1889a8\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Mode options<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You can have your LEDs just be solid, or you can have them make patterns! This is what your options for mode are:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>OFF: your LEDs are off<\/li>\n<li>SOLID: your LEDs are solid<\/li>\n<li>STROBE: your LEDs will flash a variety of colors<\/li>\n<li>BLINK: your LEDs will flicker at a steady rate<\/li>\n<li>DOUBLE_BLINK: your LEDs will flicker twice and then pause before repeating<\/li>\n<li>DIMMING: your LEDs will go from bright to dim and then back again<\/li>\n<li>PULSE: LEDs alternate between the front two arms and the back two arms<\/li>\n<li>REVERSE_PULSE: reverse of PULSE<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215d1889fa\" name=\"6a2215d1889fa\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Interval options<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>The default value for interval within each LED function is 100 milliseconds. Any other number you decide to use, from 0 to 95626825, will be counted in milliseconds.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215d188a63\" name=\"6a2215d188a63\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Examples<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Here are some examples of using LEDs in your CoDrone&#8217;s void setup code!<\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  CoDrone.begin(115200);\r\n  CoDrone.pair();\r\n  CoDrone.move(0.3);\r\n  CoDrone.setArmLED(0, 255, 255, SOLID); \/\/holds aqua color\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>In this code, the CoDrone&#8217;s arm LEDs hold the color aqua.<\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  CoDrone.begin(115200);\r\n  CoDrone.pair(); \/\/connect to previously connected CoDrone\r\n  CoDrone.move(0.3); \/\/wait 0.3 seconds\r\n\r\n  CoDrone.setArmLED(0, 255, 255, SOLID); \/\/holds aqua color\r\n\r\n  delay(100);\r\n  \r\n  CoDrone.setEyeLED(255, 0, 255, BLINK); \/\/holds magenta color\r\n}\r\n \r\nvoid loop() {}<\/pre>\n<p>In this code, the CoDrone&#8217;s eye LEDs are added, and they flicker magenta at a rate of 30 after a 100 millisecond delay.<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>Try both codes out with the colors and patterns of your choice!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215d188adf\" name=\"6a2215d188adf\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LEDs with flags<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you want to change the CoDrone&#8217;s LEDs more than once per program, there are a couple of ways to do that. One is with flags, so that your CoDrone&#8217;s LEDs will change whenever a flag is triggered. In this program, we also added buzzers so you have some idea of how your program is working.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include&lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nint Flag;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  CoDrone.begin(115200);\r\n  CoDrone.pair();\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {\r\n  byte bt1 = digitalRead(11);\r\n  byte bt4 = digitalRead(14);\r\n  byte bt8 = digitalRead(18);\r\n\r\n  if (Flag == 0) {\r\n    if (bt1) {\r\n      Flag = 1;\r\n      CoDrone.Buzz(4000, 8);\r\n      delay(300);\r\n      CoDrone.setArmLED(0, 255, 255, SOLID); \/\/holds aqua color\r\n\r\n    }\r\n  } \r\n  else if (Flag == 1) {\r\n    if (bt1) {\r\n      Flag = 0;\r\n      CoDrone.Buzz(8000, 8);\r\n      delay(300);\r\n      CoDrone.setArmLED(255, 255, 0, DIMMING); \/\/dims yellow color\r\n\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>This is the pseudocode:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Include the CoDrone library.<\/li>\n<li>Establish communication at a baud rate of 115200.<\/li>\n<li>Connect to a nearby drone.<\/li>\n<li>Establish sensors 11, 14, and 18 as inputs.<\/li>\n<li>If the flag is 0 and if sensor 11 is covered, set the flag to 1.<\/li>\n<li>Once the flag is at 1, play a sound on the buzzer, wait for 300 milliseconds, and set the CoDrone&#8217;s LEDs to dim aqua.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if the flag is at 1 and sensor 11 is covered, set the flag to 0.<\/li>\n<li>Once the flag is at 0, play a sound on the buzzer, wait for 300 milliseconds, and set the CoDrone&#8217;s LEDs to dim yellow.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>You could technically include the LED commands in the flag if statements outside of the flag events in <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">if(bt1)<\/code><code class=\"code-snippet-inline\"><\/code>, but then the LED commands will constantly be sending since they&#8217;re in void loop. If you include them within the flag events, the command will only need to be sent once and it will stay until another flag event is triggered.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215d188b5f\" name=\"6a2215d188b5f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LEDs with timers and flags<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Another way to change your CoDrone LEDs more than once per program is with timers. Again, this is easier to do with flags that trigger an event so you&#8217;re not sending the same commands over and over again.<\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nunsigned long SetTime;\r\nint ColorFlag;\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  CoDrone.begin(115200);\r\n  CoDrone.pair();\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {\r\n  if ( millis() - SetTime &gt; 1000) {\r\n    if (ColorFlag == 0) {\r\n      CoDrone.setArmLED(255, 255, 255, DIMMING); \/\/dims white color\r\n      ColorFlag = 1;\r\n    }\r\n    else if (ColorFlag == 1) {\r\n      CoDrone.setArmLED(255, 255, 0, DIMMING); \/\/dims yellow color\r\n      ColorFlag = 0;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    SetTime = millis();\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>This is the pseudocode:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Include the CoDrone library.<\/li>\n<li>Establish <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">SetTime<\/code> as an unsigned long variable and establish <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">ColorFlag<\/code> as an int variable.<\/li>\n<li>Establish communication at a baud rate of 115200.<\/li>\n<li>Connect to a nearby drone.<\/li>\n<li>If the current milliseconds minus the <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">SetTime<\/code> milliseconds are greater than 1000 and if <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">ColorFlag<\/code> is at 0, set the CoDrone LEDs to dim white and then set <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">ColorFlag<\/code> to 1.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">ColorFlag<\/code> is at 1, set the CoDrone LEDs to dim yellow and then set <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">ColorFlag<\/code> to 0.<\/li>\n<li><code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">SetTime<\/code> stores milliseconds.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215d188bc5\" name=\"6a2215d188bc5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Implementing LEDs into flight code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You can use any of these methods in your CoDrone flight codes to make your programs more flashy. Here&#8217;s an example using an autonomous timer to change the flight movements and the LEDs.<\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nunsigned long StartTime;\r\nint StartFlag;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  CoDrone.begin(115200);\r\n  CoDrone.pair();\r\n\r\n  CoDrone.takeoff();\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {\r\n  byte bt1 = digitalRead(11);\r\n\r\n  if (bt1) {\r\n    StartFlag = 1;\r\n    StartTime = millis();\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (StartFlag == 1) {\r\n    if (millis() - StartTime &lt; 1000) { \r\n      CoDrone.setEyeLED(255, 255, 255, DIMMING); \/\/dims white color\r\n      CoDrone.setThrottle(50);\r\n      CoDrone.move();\r\n    }\r\n    else if ( millis() - StartTime &lt; 3000) {\r\n      CoDrone.setEyeLED(0, 0, 255, DIMMING); \/\/dims blue color\r\n      CoDrone.setPitch(50);  \r\n      CoDrone.setThrottle(0);\r\n      CoDrone.move();\r\n    }\r\n    else { \r\n      CoDrone.land();\r\n      StartFlag = 0; \r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215d188c32\" name=\"6a2215d188c32\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p><strong>Challenge: Double rainbow<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Write a CoDrone flight code with additional LED commands!<\/p>\n<p><strong>Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Make the eyes cycle through\u00a03 different colors.<\/li>\n<li>Make the arms switch between 2 colors.<\/li>\n<li>Make sure that you can still control your CoDrone normally with your controller.<\/li>\n<li>Don&#8217;t forget a kill switch so you can stop your CoDrone at any time!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"activity2__spacer\">\n<div class=\"activity2__question\">\n<div class=\"styled-checkbox activity2__button-checkbox\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 LED settings [vc_column_text]The easiest way to change your LEDs is to do it in void setup. This will change the LEDs' colors and patterns before your program&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-leds\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1749,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":804,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1737,1815,1782,1848,1793,1826,1482,853,694,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2195,2163,2164,2165,2120,2122],"class_list":["post-1175","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-advanced","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-pro","lesson-tag-led","lesson-tag-programming","module-advanced","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1175","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1175\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1176,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1175\/revisions\/1176"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1749"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1175"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1175"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1175"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}